	(text "IcepiZero_AD9280_AD9708_2x12  --  HS-AD/DA V2.0 AD9280 ADC + AD9708 DAC\n\nJ1 is a 2x20 socket on the BOTTOM of the board; it mates the\nIcepi Zero's 40-pin header.  J2 is a pin header, pins up on the TOP for the\nconverter module.  Both are 2.54 mm.  GND1 and GND2 are plated\nholes on the ground pour, one in each margin, for a wire to the\nmodule's own GND / AGND / DGND holes -- its header grounds are\ntoo few to be a return path for sixteen switching signals.\n\nModule label / gateware name -> Icepi header pin / GPIO /\nECP5 ball.  The two names differ where the module's silkscreen\ndoes not use this project's; the .lpf uses the second one, so\nthat one Verilog source builds for every board in the family.\n\n    AD0      ad0    pin 7   GPIO4    R1\n    AD1      ad1    pin 11  GPIO17   R3\n    AD2      ad2    pin 12  GPIO18   N4\n    AD3      ad3    pin 13  GPIO27   P3\n    AD4      ad4    pin 15  GPIO22   P2\n    AD5      ad5    pin 16  GPIO23   M2\n    AD6      ad6    pin 18  GPIO24   L1\n    AD7      ad7    pin 19  GPIO10   L2\n    ACLK     aclk   pin 21  GPIO9    J1\n    DCLK     dclk   pin 23  GPIO11   G2\n    DA7      da7    pin 24  GPIO8    H2\n    DA6      da6    pin 26  GPIO7    G1\n    DA5      da5    pin 29  GPIO5    E1\n    DA4      da4    pin 31  GPIO6    F3\n    DA3      da3    pin 32  GPIO12   J3\n    DA2      da2    pin 33  GPIO13   E3\n    DA1      da1    pin 35  GPIO19   E4\n    DA0      da0    pin 37  GPIO26   D4\n\nPins marked ? on the module carry no silkscreen label.\nThey are left unconnected on purpose -- see README.md."
		(at 15.0000 15.0000 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.40 1.40)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "b1361500-e6a8-5421-9494-e05e1be56472")
	)
